course: dictionary
lesson: 3928
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which one you need. «The frozen lake was thick enough to hold a skater.» Here frozen means turned into hard ice, because the lake is the thing that froze.
explain: «Frozen peas were kept in the freezer.» Now frozen means kept very cold so the food lasts longer. The word is the same, but the clue is freezer, so you know it is about food, not ice.
explain: «My fingers were frozen after the snowball fight.» Here frozen means very cold. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits best.
explain: Frozen is a form of the verb freeze: freeze, froze, frozen. We use frozen after has, have or was, as in «The pond has frozen.» Froze is the past tense, so «The pond froze» is correct, but not «The pond frozen».
fact: Frozen means turned into ice or made hard by cold, as in «a frozen lake».
fact: Water becomes frozen, or solid ice, at 0 °C.
fact: Frozen food is kept very cold in a freezer so it lasts longer.
fact: Frozen can also mean not able to move, for example from fear.
fact: Never walk or skate on a frozen pond unless an adult says the ice is safe, because ice can be thin and break.
exercise: «The frozen lake was thick enough to hold a skater.» In this sentence, what does frozen mean? | Very hungry | *Turned into hard ice | Not able to move | Kept cold in a freezer
exercise: «Ben stood frozen with fear when the dog barked.» What does frozen mean here? | Very warm | Kept cold in a freezer | *Not able to move | Turned into ice
exercise: «Frozen peas were kept in the freezer.» Find and copy the word that tells you frozen means kept cold so it lasts. | *freezer | frozen | kept | peas
test: «Mum took the frozen pizza out of the freezer.» What does frozen mean? | *Kept very cold in a freezer so it lasts longer | Unable to move with fear | Very wet | Turned into ice on the pond
test: Which sentence uses frozen to mean very cold? | «The horse was frozen with fear.» | *«My hands are frozen after the snow.» | «The frozen pond is safe to skate on.»
exam: In «life survives in boiling vents and frozen lakes», what does frozen mean? | Very hungry | Not able to move | Kept cold in a freezer | *Turned into solid ice by very cold weather
